{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-11_12-49-23-hashicorp_raft-real-run; cat research.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"run_id\": \"d448760a0cf34c6582caa2c65044976a\",\n  \"method\": \"audit-products-v62\",\n  \"allocation\": {\n    \"seconds\": 1044.042529373,\n    \"agent_calls\": 78,\n    \"experiments\": 39\n  },\n  \"source_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-11_12-49-23-hashicorp_raft-real-run/agent-source\",\n  \"draft_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-11_12-49-23-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft\",\n  \"state_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-11_12-49-23-hashicorp_raft-real-run/state.json\",\n  \"submission_schema\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-11_12-49-23-hashicorp_raft-real-run/submission.schema.json\",\n  \"method_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-11_12-49-23-hashicorp_raft-real-run/audit-method.md\",\n  \"directed_question\": null,\n  \"activity_focus\": [],\n  \"investigations\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b02f82dfc4024a638ae4ecbdcb18b1fc-question-0\",\n      \"version\": 1,\n      \"question\": \"When a follower installs a snapshot while its persisted log already ends above the snapshot's LastLogIndex, does the follower's last-log report allow the leader's next AppendEntries (PrevLogEntry = snapshot index) to be accepted, or does the leader loop re-transferring the same snapshot with no follower progress?\",\n      \"hypothesis\": \"installSnapshot restores the FSM, sets lastApplied/lastSnapshot/configuration and compacts logs at or below req.LastLogIndex, but never truncates log entries above req.LastLogIndex and never calls setLastLog. The cached lastLogIndex/lastLogTerm therefore keep the stale suffix, so getLastEntry reports (staleLast, staleTerm) instead of (snapshotIndex, snapshotTerm) whenever lastLogIndex > lastSnapshotIndex. appendEntries then fails the PrevLogEntry==lastIdx branch and either logs.GetLog errors (entries compacted) or returns the stale term, so it rejects with NoRetryBackoff. The leader lowers nextIndex by one (resp.LastLog+1 is above nextIndex-1, so min picks nextIndex-1), and once nextIndex-1 falls below the leader's compacted first index setupAppendEntries returns ErrLogNotFound and the leader re-sends the identical snapshot.\",\n      \"discriminator\": \"Run the same 3-node in-memory scenario twice: with the isolated node's pre-reconnect last log index below the replacement leader's snapshot index (control, no stale suffix) and above it (case, stale suffix). If the explanation holds the control converges after one install, while the case leaves the isolated node stuck at the snapshot index with leader commit index above it and repeated identical snapshot installs. If the case also converges, the stale-suffix explanation is refuted and the harness or predicate must be revisited.\",\n      \"disposition\": \"active\",\n      \"parent_id\": null,\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"install_snapshot\",\n        \"get_last_entry\",\n        \"append_prev_check\",\n        \"set_previous_log\",\n        \"replicate_to\",\n        \"send_latest_snapshot\"\n      ],\n      \"counterevidence\": [],\n      \"limitations\": [],\n      \"resume_conditions\": [],\n      \"knowledge\": [],\n      \"open_gaps\": [],\n      \"latest_execution\": {\n        \"id\": \"61befa27ce114c8097c8bdfa597e9ee5\",\n        \"experiment_id\": \"b02f82dfc4024a638ae4ecbdcb18b1fc-experiment\",\n        \"status\": \"completed\",\n        \"exit_code\": 0,\n        \"record\": \"logs/61befa27ce114c8097c8bdfa597e9ee5/check.json\",\n        \"observations\": \"logs/61befa27ce114c8097c8bdfa597e9ee5/observations.json\"\n      },\n      \"latest_interpretation\": null,\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"investigations\",\n        \"id\": \"b02f82dfc4024a638ae4ecbdcb18b1fc-question-0\"\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"knowledge\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b02f82dfc4024a638ae4ecbdcb18b1fc-knowledge-0\",\n      \"revision\": 1,\n      \"kind\": \"behavior\",\n      \"statement\": \"(*Raft).installSnapshot restores the received snapshot into the FSM, sets lastApplied=req.LastLogIndex, sets lastSnapshot=(req.LastLogIndex,req.LastLogTerm), overwrites the latest and committed configuration, then removes or compacts only logs at or below req.LastLogIndex (removeOldLogs for a MonotonicLogStore, otherwise compactLogs). It never calls setLastLog and never truncates log entries above req.LastLogIndex, so the cached lastLogIndex/lastLogTerm retain any pre-existing suffix.\",\n      \"conditions\": \"A follower handles an InstallSnapshotRequest and its persisted log already contains entries at indices greater than req.LastLogIndex, for example an uncommitted suffix written by an earlier leader term.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"install_snapshot_decl\"\n      ],\n      \"executions\": {},\n      \"operation_id\": \"b02f82dfc4024a638ae4ecbdcb18b1fc\",\n      \"uses\": [],\n      \"last_correction\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b02f82dfc4024a638ae4ecbdcb18b1fc-knowledge-1\",\n      \"revision\": 1,\n      \"kind\": \"behavior\",\n      \"statement\": \"(*raftState).getLastEntry returns (lastLogIndex,lastLogTerm) whenever lastLogIndex >= lastSnapshotIndex, and returns (lastSnapshotIndex,lastSnapshotTerm) only when the cached log index is below the snapshot index. After a snapshot install that leaves a longer persisted log, the follower therefore reports the stale tail index and term rather than the snapshot index and term.\",\n      \"conditions\": \"lastLogIndex > lastSnapshotIndex on the local raftState, which holds after installSnapshot when the log was not truncated above the snapshot index.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"get_last_entry\"\n      ],\n      \"executions\": {},\n      \"operation_id\": \"b02f82dfc4024a638ae4ecbdcb18b1fc\",\n      \"uses\": [],\n      \"last_correction\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b02f82dfc4024a638ae4ecbdcb18b1fc-knowledge-2\",\n      \"revision\": 1,\n      \"kind\": \"behavior\",\n      \"statement\": \"(*Raft).appendEntries verifies a.PrevLogEntry by comparing it to getLastEntry; if they differ it reads logs.GetLog(a.PrevLogEntry). A missing entry or a differing term sets resp.NoRetryBackoff=true and rejects the request without truncating the local log.\",\n      \"conditions\": \"A follower receives an AppendEntriesRequest with a.PrevLogEntry > 0.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"append_prev_check\"\n      ],\n      \"executions\": {},\n      \"operation_id\": \"b02f82dfc4024a638ae4ecbdcb18b1fc\",\n      \"uses\": [],\n      \"last_correction\": null\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b02f82dfc4024a638ae4ecbdcb18b1fc-knowledge-3\",\n      \"revision\": 1,\n      \"kind\": \"behavior\",\n      \"statement\": \"(*Raft).replicateTo advances s.nextIndex to max(min(s.nextIndex-1, resp.LastLog+1), 1) on a rejected AppendEntries, so a follower that reports a higher LastLog than the leader's nextIndex causes nextIndex to decrease by one; when setupAppendEntries returns ErrLogNotFound it goes to SEND_SNAP and sendLatestSnapshot re-sends the newest snapshot and sets nextIndex=meta.Index+1 on success.\",\n      \"conditions\": \"The follower keeps rejecting AppendEntries and its reported LastLog stays above the leader's nextIndex.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"replicate_to\",\n        \"send_latest_snapshot\"\n      ],\n      \"executions\": {},\n      \"operation_id\": \"b02f82dfc4024a638ae4ecbdcb18b1fc\",\n      \"uses\": [],\n      \"last_correction\": null\n    }\n  ],\n  \"experiments\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"b02f82dfc4024a638ae4ecbdcb18b1fc-experiment\",\n      \"investigation_id\": \"b02f82dfc4024a638ae4ecbdcb18b1fc-question-0\",\n      \"previous_id\": null,\n      \"basis\": \"f